### Title
Ensure v3 packages are available when mixing sharded and unsharded repos

### Why
This is a bug fix so that users may use monolithic and sharded channels with v3 repodata.

### Platforms
- [x] Windows
- [x] macOS
- [x] Linux

### Prerequisites
Setup a demo monolithic channel with wheel records (uses v3 repodata). With conda-pypi install (`conda install -n base conda-pypi`):

```
pip download --dest /tmp/mychannel/noarch pyfig
conda pypi index /tmp/mychannel
```

### Steps
1. Ensure that conda can search the channels for pyfig. conda should show the same version of pyfig from the channel named `mychannel`.
```
 $ conda search --override-channels -c file://tmp/mychannel -c conda-forge pyfig 

Loading channels: done
# Name                       Version           Build  Channel             
pyfig                          1.0.2  py3_none_any_0  mychannel 
```

2. Try creating an environment with pyfig. conda should be installing pyfig from the channel named `mychannel`.
```
$ conda create -n test --override-channels -c file://tmp/mychannel -c conda-forge --dry-run pyfig
. . .
The following NEW packages will be INSTALLED:
. . .
  pyfig              mychannel/noarch::pyfig-1.0.2-py3_none_any_0 
. . .
```

### Pass criteria
* There are no failures running the steps above, and all checks pass.

